        "content": "<p>ChihweiLHBird opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14880\">PR #14880</a> from <code>ChihweiLHBird:zhiwei/post-return-timeout</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>-W timeout</code> also bounded how long a WASIp3 component instance may keep running after all of its requests have produced responses, for example while it is still streaming a response body, so a short request timeout cut off long-lived streams. Add <code>--post-return-timeout</code> to bound that phase on its own. It defaults to <code>-W timeout</code>, so behavior is unchanged unless it is set.</p>\n<p>Like <code>-W timeout</code>, setting the option runs blocking WASI filesystem calls on background threads and enables epoch interruption, so the deadline is enforced while the guest is blocked in a filesystem call or never yields. <code>RunCommon::configure_wasip2</code> now takes the blocking decision as a parameter, since <code>run</code> and <code>serve</code> derive it differently.</p>\n</blockquote>",
